-- title:
--   The ambient scalar isomorphism carries the vacuum state
-- statement:
--   Let $u,v$ be nonzero real numbers with $u^2+v^2=1$. Let $\mathcal A(u,v)$ be the ambient von Neumann algebra of the weighted Fock model with edges labelled by $\mathbb N$, with vacuum state $\omega$, and let $\Psi$ be the isomorphism of $\mathcal A(u,v)$ onto the scalar Gaussian algebra generated by the scalar system with root $\Omega$. For $T\in\mathcal A(u,v)$,
--
--   $$\langle\Omega,\Psi(T)\Omega\rangle=\omega(T).$$
--
--   This shows that the identification with the free Gaussian algebra is trace-preserving.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The statement is verbatim from OpenAI's Lean development, with the listed `Definitions` imported in place of the upstream modules; the definitions are supporting code for this statement.
-- source:
--   OpenAI, An isomorphism of the free group factors, September 23, 2026, https://github.com/openai/math (paper: preprints/An-isomorphism-of-the-free-group-factors-September-23-2026/An-isomorphism-of-the-free-group-factors-September-23-2026.pdf; Lean: lean/OAI/Analysis/FreeGroupFactor and lean/OAI/Analysis/InterpolatedFactors, Apache License 2.0); Lean declaration `OAI.FreeGroupFactorMain.WeightedFock.ambientScalarIso_trace`, https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/OAI/Analysis/InterpolatedFactors/WeightedCorner.lean#L186

